    {
      "document_id": "251",
      "explanation": "Relied on clarification item (7): electoral campaigns where specific gun laws are the substantive issue. The editorial urges gun-owner voter registration by citing specific measures decided by narrow margins—the 1989 California Assembly semi-automatic ban, the 1990 New Jersey Senate ban, the DeConcini bill, and California's Proposition 117—making gun legislation the substantive subject of the political action, not incidental electioneering.",
